      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "IFMcCnrT5h_-oE3d7sG4l",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 459.41386642187507,
      "y": 1354,
      "width": 560.62353515625,
      "height": 320,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 222754995,
      "version": 1638,
      "versionNonce": 802464436,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794994369672,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Registers: the add uses them directly. No load.\nAt least 100x the bandwidth of global memory and at least\n10x less energy per access. \n\nShared memory: needs a load, but stays on-chip, so the wait is short.\nSeveral process blocks can read and write it at the same time.\n\nGlobal memory: needs a load and a trip off-chip. Slowest, and it uses up\nbandwidth, so the compute-to-global-memory-access ratio goes up.\n\nRegisters are limited: too many per thread lowers occupancy \n(one of the four pools that fills up on an SM and determines\nthe number of blocks that can fit on an SM).\n\nRule of thumb: registers, then shared memory, then global memory.\nLoad from the global memory once, then reuse on-chip.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Registers: the add uses them directly. No load.\nAt least 100x the bandwidth of global memory and at least\n10x less energy per access. \n\nShared memory: needs a load, but stays on-chip, so the wait is short.\nSeveral process blocks can read and write it at the same time.\n\nGlobal memory: needs a load and a trip off-chip. Slowest, and it uses up\nbandwidth, so the compute-to-global-memory-access ratio goes up.\n\nRegisters are limited: too many per thread lowers occupancy \n(one of the four pools that fills up on an SM and determines\nthe number of blocks that can fit on an SM).\n\nRule of thumb: registers, then shared memory, then global memory.\nLoad from the global memory once, then reuse on-chip.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "sF_jpsBTv2iRV_8PMGT2n",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1048.6480175859379,
      "y": 1483,
      "width": 481.487548828125,
      "height": 160,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 974827357,
      "version": 593,
      "versionNonce": 1300102269,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794841176911,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A processing block = one dispatcher + its own group of cores.\nIt is hardware inside an SM.\n\nAn SM is split into several processing blocks.\n\nThe dispatcher picks a ready warp and issues one \ninstruction to all 32 of its threads; the cores\ncarry it out.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A processing block = one dispatcher + its own group of cores.\nIt is hardware inside an SM.\n\nAn SM is split into several processing blocks.\n\nThe dispatcher picks a ready warp and issues one \ninstruction to all 32 of its threads; the cores\ncarry it out.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-tnr0UotyiyhEbyYqgSU_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1048.6480175859376,
      "y": 1370,
      "width": 705.50341796875,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1277372477,
      "version": 877,
      "versionNonce": 2134960695,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794841688642,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Registers are the memory of the memory hierarchy associated with individual threads.\nThey are the lowest level of the memory hierarchy, which store information manipulated by\na single thread.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Registers are the memory of the memory hierarchy associated with individual threads.\nThey are the lowest level of the memory hierarchy, which store information manipulated by\na single thread.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
